      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report the case of a 77-year-old man, with nefopam postoperative analgesia, who developed subacute neurological symptoms, whereas he had profound hypoprotidemia and acute renal failure. Chronological, semiological and bibliographical criteria are in favour of causality assessment. The plasma nefopam concentration (135 ng/ml) during the neurological symptoms is another argument."},
